---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ENTITY_STATEMENT } from '../data/site.js';
---

<Base
  title="Experience"
  path="/experience"
  description={`${ENTITY_STATEMENT} Structured career timeline with dates, titles, and outcomes, plus a machine-readable resume.`}
>
  <h1>Experience</h1>
  <p class="kicker">
    A machine-readable version of this record lives at
    <a href="/resume.json">/resume.json</a> (JSON Resume schema).
  </p>

  <h2>Timeline</h2>
  <dl class="record">
    <div>
      <dt>VP of Product, Deep Media · January 2025 – present</dt>
      <dd>
        Remote. Deep Media is a content security infrastructure company. I own
        product strategy and roadmap across the platform: Shield, the detection and API layer built
        around the Content Genome engine, Skills, the composable capability layer, and Guardian,
        autonomous AI agents that proactively investigate fraud, disinformation, terrorist and
        violent extremist content, brand safety, NCII, and threat intelligence across the surface,
        deep, and dark web. Investigations that previously took weeks now take hours, with
        audit-ready output built for regulators and courts. Stood up all-layer web threat
        intelligence, built the dark web collection feed that opened a $2B+ addressable segment in
        government and brand risk monitoring, and closed a custom data feed agreement with a
        government contractor to monitor extremist content and weapons-related incitement. Ran
        product and go-to-market as a one-person team in year one, and built the AI agent stack
        that runs my own operations. Deep Media's work is trusted by the U.S. Department of Defense
        and major technology platforms.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Director, Product &amp; Business Development, Trust Stamp · May 2023 – December 2025</dt>
      <dd>
        Biometric authentication and synthetic identity detection for financial services. First
        North American go-to-market hire: built a $10MM+ pipeline from a flat territory across
        financial institutions, social platforms, and dating apps, and hired and managed seven U.S.
        sales reps. Owned the deepfake detection API end to end, from authoring the PRD to packaging
        detection for financial crimes, KYC, and identity fraud use cases. Served as the technical
        closer with CISOs and security architects, and authored 50-page technical responses to
        federal RFIs on synthetic identity detection, biometric liveness, and AI-enabled fraud
        threat modeling.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Enterprise Account Executive, Veriff · November 2021 – May 2023</dt>
      <dd>
        Global identity verification platform. Promoted from team lead to a quota-carrying
        enterprise role in eight months. Worked a $4MM+ enterprise pipeline and beat quota by 25%
        or more for five consecutive quarters, building the ROI models that opened budget where
        none existed. Ran six-month procurement cycles end to end with
        General Counsels, CISOs, and Heads of Fraud at financial institutions, and built deep
        expertise in KYC and AML-adjacent identity workflows and the operational reality of fraud
        teams in regulated industries.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Sales Development Team Lead, Veriff · March 2021 – October 2021</dt>
      <dd>
        Veriff's first U.S. hire. Opened the U.S. market with no playbook, wrote the sales
        development strategy from scratch, and scaled the team from one to twelve in under a year.
        The team generated $50MM+ in new pipeline in its first twelve months.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Sales Development Representative, SheerID · June 2020 – March 2021</dt>
      <dd>
        Portland, OR. Mapped buying committees across 200 target accounts to book meetings with
        VP-level marketing buyers at Fortune 500 retail brands.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Founder &amp; CEO, Root Connection · March 2015 – March 2021</dt>
      <dd>
        Portland, OR. Founded a research and design firm and grew it from zero to $1MM in annual
        revenue in two years, then ran it profitably for six. Sold 50+ contracts worth $100K or more
        each by working multi-stakeholder deals across owners, contractors, and municipal planners.
        Built the marketing engine (search, ads, content, trade shows), ran operations and
        accounting, managed crews and 15+ vendors, advised regulated agriculture clients on
        licensing and compliance, and wrote and won grants for agricultural research projects.
        Everything I now do in product and sales, I learned first by having to make payroll.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Sales &amp; Marketing Lead, One Green World · June 2015 – June 2017</dt>
      <dd>
        Portland, OR, concurrent with Root Connection. Managed a $500K+ wholesale book of business
        and drove B2B retail expansion for a specialty nursery.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Clinical Research Coordinator, Oregon Health &amp; Science University · November 2007 – February 2013</dt>
      <dd>
        Portland, OR. Coordinated Phase 3 clinical trials: protocol adherence, human-subject
        scheduling and consent, procurement, and cross-department coordination in a regulated
        research environment. Bilingual point of contact for patients and families.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Earlier · 2003 – 2008</dt>
      <dd>
        Assistant manager of an automotive service location, responsible for hiring, training,
        budget, inventory, and sales. Program and budget lead for a community health nonprofit
        chapter working in the U.S. and Honduras.
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <h2>Recognition</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Winner, Safety by Design Trust &amp; Safety Hackathon, April 2024, with team FaceLock.
    </li>
    <li>
      Participant in the inaugural Trust &amp; Safety Hackathon in San Francisco (July 2023) and the
      Paris edition (2024).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Credentials</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      B.S., Horticulture (Research Option), Oregon State University. Dean's List, A.L. Strand
      Memorial Scholarship in Entomology, OSU Research Fellow, Pi Alpha Xi Honor Society,
      Permaculture Research Institute.
    </li>
    <li>Languages: English (native), Spanish (conversational).</li>
    <li>
      Apprenti Marketing Apprenticeship, registered with the U.S. Department of Labor, completed
      January 9, 2026.
    </li>
  </ul>
</Base>
